On the reference to Khyung as "slang pa/slang pha/slang pha ba" (understood as a regionalism for "glang pa/glang pha ba," see [WL39GVT5]: 940.</note></person><person xml:id="person3816"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar byang chub ye shes</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཨར་བྱང་ཆུབ་ཡེ་ཤེས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ar</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang chub ye shes</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">shag kya'i dge slong byang ye</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">a ro byang chub ye shes</persName><birth notBefore="1054-01-01" notAfter="1056-12-31">after 1054 before 1056</birth><death notBefore="1134-01-01" notAfter="1194-12-31">after 1134 before 1194</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2552</idno><idno type="APIS">3816</idno><note type="comment">Dates according to [2V6H2FBU]: 24, n. 70 ("Since Ar was invited as a dge bshes to a monastery in 1076, it is hard to believe that he was not at least 20 years old, which would put his birth-date at least in 1056. The last trace of his existence is in 1144 when he took over the head of rgyal lha khang.").</note></person><person xml:id="person3817"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal pa bsregs ston</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཉལ་པ་བསྲེགས་སྟོན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">snyal ba bsregs ston</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gnyal sregs</persName><birth notBefore="1050-01-01">after 1050</birth><death notAfter="1230-12-31">before 1230</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">3817</idno></person><person xml:id="person3827"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brom ston rgyal ba'i 'byung gnas</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འབྲོམ་སྟོན་རྒྱལ་བའི་འབྱུང་གནས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes ston pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge bshes ston pa chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge' bshes ston pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brum ston rgyal ba'i 'byung gnas</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'brom</persName><birth notBefore="1004-01-01" notAfter="1005-12-31">after 1004 before 1005</birth><death notBefore="1064-01-01" notAfter="1064-12-31">1064</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2557</idno><idno type="APIS">3827</idno><note type="comment">Celibate householder from the Byang region, chief disciple of Atiśa (ID: 3745) ([Q922IUFM]: 30). &#13;
&#13;
dGe 'dun grub pa (ID:7060) is renowned as his reincarnation and his 'Brom ston-like qualities are described ([BKUHJCNA]: 787-790).</note></person><person xml:id="person3880"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro ston bdud rtsi grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྲོ་སྟོན་བདུད་རྩི་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">snar thang mkhan po a rmi ta kir ti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro mo che ba bdud rtsi grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gra ston chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">amṛtakīrti</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gro mo che</persName><birth notBefore="1153-01-01" notAfter="1153-12-31">1153</birth><death notBefore="1232-01-01" notAfter="1232-12-31">1232</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P2271</idno><idno type="APIS">3880</idno><note type="comment">Fourth abbot of sNar thang (ID:4411). On his life see [NTGHCZA8]: 34-51.</note></person><person xml:id="person3924"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rdo ston shes rab grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">རྡོ་སྟོན་ཤེས་རབ་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">g.yas chen po shes rab grags</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">dge slong shes rab grags</persName><birth notBefore="1127-01-01" notAfter="1127-12-31">1127</birth><death notBefore="1185-01-01" notAfter="1185-12-31">1185</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4088</idno><idno type="APIS">3924</idno></person><person xml:id="person3925"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gtum ston blo gros grags</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གཏུམ་སྟོན་བློ་གྲོས་གྲགས</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">stum ston blo gros grags pa</persName><birth notBefore="1106-01-01" notAfter="1106-1